path: .claude/guides/rule-extracts/recommendation-quality.md
expect:
family: command-vs-data — a FENCED example is documentation of the violation
note: COPIED BYTE-FOR-BYTE from the live extract's DO/DO-NOT block. Without the
  fenced-block strip this file is the detector's loudest true positive in the whole
  repo — it would fire on the rule's own documentation of the thing it forbids, every
  time anyone edited the extract. Both DO-NOT tables are inside the fence; so is the
  DO table. Same class as "a heredoc'd or quoted example stays silent" in the
  merge-separation guard.
